gaps.proposedFix:
Encode: { "varint": {"encoding":"mqtt7","minBytes":1,"maxBytes":4,"minimal":true}, "value":"len(group:rest)" }
Decode: { "varint": {"encoding":"mqtt7","maxBytes":4,"minimal":true}, "as":"remainingLength" }
Engine consequence that must be specified with it: a variable-width placeholder means downstream byte offsets shift during pass 2, so any `len(from:A to:B)` spanning a varint needs fixed-point iteration (encode -> widen -> re-encode). Termination is provable: width is monotonically non-decreasing in the value and bounded by maxBytes, so the loop runs at most maxBytes times. Must be a fieldKind, not a converter — a converter cannot change pass 1's width-reservation contract.

{ "bytes": "<lenExpr>", "as":"x", "via":"utf8" }  // decode: consume lenExpr bytes, optionally pipe through one converter
{ "bytes": "capture.clientIdLen", "as":"clientId", "via":"utf8" }
Encode form is the existing { "value":"inputs.clientId | utf8" }, so this is purely a decode-side symmetry fix.

Add a nesting wrapper whose span is implicitly its own children, so no name is needed:
{ "lengthPrefixed": {"prefix":"u16be"}, "fields":[ {"value":"r.topic | utf8"} ] }
Inside `each` this is iteration-safe by construction. It also removes the two-objects-plus-a-unique-group-name boilerplate from every string in CONNECT. Decode form: { "lengthPrefixed":{"prefix":"u16be"}, "via":"utf8", "as":"topic" }. This single fix subsumes half of gap 2.

"connected": {
  "heartbeat": { "send":"mqttPingreq", "everyMs":"inputs.keepAliveSeconds * 1000",
                 "resetOnAnyTx": true, "expect":"mqttPingresp",
                 "missTolerance": 1, "onMiss":"tcpClosed" },
  "timeoutMs": "inputs.keepAliveSeconds * 1500", "onTimeout":"tcpClosed" }
Also: allow expressions in `timeoutMs` (currently shown only as a literal), and exempt heartbeat loops from the loop:{max<=64} packet bound — a heartbeat is bounded by session duration, not by hop count.

"seq": { "id":"mqttPacketId", "width":"u16", "min":1, "max":65535, "wrap":true,
         "scope":"session", "releaseOn":"mqttSuback.packetId" }
referenced as "seq.mqttPacketId.next". `releaseOn` is what makes in-flight uniqueness (rather than global uniqueness) expressible.
